From: REIMU <reimu@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] HID: never block on the keyboard, release on client exit, no stray Shift

- The keyboard was opened blocking: while the host does not take a report
  (off, suspended, its driver unbound) the next write() waits forever and
  with it the whole loop, video included. Both fds are non-blocking now; a
  report waits up to 50 ms for the host to take the previous one (f_hid has
  one in flight), then it is dropped (logged once).
- A write error other than EAGAIN closes the fd; the next report opens the
  device again (a gadget unbound and bound again).
- A VNC client going releases every key and button it held.
- The wakeup packet (a Shift press) went out on every video open, mode
  changes included, with or without a client: now only with a client.

---
--- a/ikvm_input.cpp
+++ b/ikvm_input.cpp
@@ -5,6 +5,7 @@
